<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José María Córdova</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1799–1829</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José María Córdova was a general of the wars of independence from Antioquia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>. He distinguished himself at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyaca-department">Boyacá</a> and especially at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayacucho">Ayacucho</a> in 1824, where he led the decisive attack. Opposing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>'s dictatorship and the plans for a monarchy, he rose in revolt in Antioquia in 1829 and was killed after his defeat at El Santuario.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-maria-cordova.jpg" alt="José María Córdova" width="320" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José María Espinosa · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Mar%C3%ADa_C%C3%B3rdova._An%C3%B3nimo,_ca._1840._Colecci%C3%B3n_Museo_Nacional_de_Colombia._Reg._350.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
